1. A system comprising:  

   one or more beacon devices disposed within an indoor environment, each beacon device being configured to wirelessly transmit beacon information associated with a respective location within the indoor environment;  

   one or more mobile devices, each mobile device comprising at least one wireless receiver, at least one processor, and memory storing instructions that, when executed by the at least one processor, cause the mobile device to receive the beacon information from at least one of the one or more beacon devices while the mobile device is located within the indoor environment;  

   a content management system configured to store a plurality of content items and a plurality of rules associated with delivery of the plurality of content items;  

   wherein the plurality of rules define triggering criteria based at least in part on one or more of: a location of the mobile device determined using the received beacon information, an occurrence of an event, satisfaction of one or more conditions, and one or more results generated from data associated with the mobile device, a user of the mobile device, the indoor environment, or interaction with previously provided content; and  

   wherein the mobile device and/or the content management system is configured to evaluate at least a portion of the plurality of rules using the received beacon information and, in response to determining that the triggering criteria of at least one rule are satisfied, cause corresponding content from the plurality of content items to be presented, stored, transmitted, modified, unlocked, or otherwise made available via the mobile device.

A method for distributing content associated with an indoor space and an area proximate to the indoor space, the method comprising:

deploying a plurality of short-range wireless beacons at predetermined locations within the indoor space and optionally within the nearby area, each beacon being configured to transmit a beacon signal comprising beacon identification information;

receiving, by a portable electronic device located within reception range of at least one of the plurality of beacons, the beacon signal transmitted by the at least one beacon;

obtaining, by the portable electronic device, beacon information based on the received beacon signal, the beacon information including at least one of a beacon identifier, a signal strength value, a timestamp, a device location estimate, or an identifier associated with the indoor space;

transmitting, by the portable electronic device, the beacon information to a remote content distribution system over a communication channel different from the short-range wireless channel used by the beacon, the different communication channel comprising, for example, a cellular data connection, Wi-Fi connection, wired network connection, or other packet-based network connection;

determining, by the remote content distribution system, a location, zone, proximity state, movement path, or contextual condition of the portable electronic device based at least in part on the beacon information received from the portable electronic device;

selecting, by the remote content distribution system, content associated with the determined location, zone, proximity state, movement path, or contextual condition, the content comprising at least one of promotional content, informational content, navigation content, safety content, product-related content, event content, access-related content, or interactive media; and

causing delivery of the selected content to the portable electronic device or to another output device associated with the indoor space or nearby area.

In some implementations, the beacons are Bluetooth Low Energy beacons, ultra-wideband beacons, Wi-Fi beacons, near-field communication transmitters, optical beacons, acoustic beacons, or other local transmitters configured to broadcast locally receivable identifiers without establishing a network session with the portable electronic device. The different communication channel used by the portable electronic device to communicate with the remote content distribution system may be independent of the beacon transmission channel and may support bidirectional communication between the portable electronic device and the remote content distribution system.

The method may further comprise maintaining, by the remote content distribution system, a mapping between beacon identifiers and physical locations, logical zones, content categories, rules, or campaigns. Upon receipt of beacon information from the portable electronic device, the remote content distribution system may compare the beacon information to the mapping to determine the portable electronic device’s presence in a particular room, aisle, exhibit area, store section, entry zone, queue area, transportation platform, venue region, or outdoor-adjacent area.

The beacon information transmitted by the portable electronic device may include signal strength measurements for multiple received beacon signals. The remote content distribution system may process the signal strength measurements to estimate relative proximity to respective beacons, triangulate or multilaterate a position of the portable electronic device, determine whether the portable electronic device has entered or exited a zone, or infer a direction of travel. The system may further apply filtering, thresholding, confidence scoring, time averaging, or machine-learning-based classification to reduce false detections.

The selected content may be personalized based on user profile data, device attributes, language preferences, transaction history, visit history, calendar data, ticketing data, loyalty account data, subscription status, or consent settings associated with the portable electronic device or a user thereof. The remote content distribution system may also consider environmental information, time of day, crowd density, event schedules, inventory data, security conditions, weather conditions, or operator-defined rules when selecting content.

In one embodiment, the portable electronic device receives a beacon identifier from a beacon located near an entrance to the indoor space, sends the beacon identifier to the remote content distribution system using a cellular or Wi-Fi data connection, and receives from the remote content distribution system content relevant to the entrance area. As the portable electronic device moves through the indoor space and detects additional beacons, the portable electronic device transmits updated beacon information to the remote content distribution system, which dynamically changes the content provided to correspond to the portable electronic device’s updated position or context.

The method may further comprise authenticating the portable electronic device before delivering content, encrypting communications between the portable electronic device and the remote content distribution system, anonymizing or pseudonymizing device identifiers, storing consent records, and enforcing privacy preferences associated with location-based content delivery.

The method may be implemented by a system comprising the plurality of beacons, the portable electronic device executing a client application or browser-based process, and one or more servers forming the remote content distribution system. The one or more servers may include a beacon registry, a location inference engine, a content selection engine, a campaign management module, and a delivery interface configured to transmit selected content to the portable electronic device or to another device, such as a display, kiosk, speaker, point-of-sale terminal, access gate, or signage controller.

The method enables beacon-based localization and content distribution while avoiding the need for the beacons themselves to maintain wide-area network connectivity. The portable electronic device functions as a relay between the locally transmitted beacon information and the remote content distribution system, using a communication channel separate from the beacon communication channel to request, trigger, or facilitate delivery of contextually relevant content.
